# Project Structure

Organize code by feature under `src/features/{feature}/`. Shared code lives in top-level folders.

```
src/
├── features/{feature}/
│   ├── api/           # Feature-specific hooks and fetchers
│   ├── components/    # Feature-only components
│   ├── types.ts
│   └── index.ts       # Public barrel export
├── components/        # Shared UI components
├── hooks/             # Shared hooks
├── api/               # Shared API client, queryKeys, fetchers
└── styles/            # Global tokens and themes
```

## Conventions

- One component per folder: `{Name}/index.tsx`, `{Name}.css.ts`, `types.ts`
- File names: PascalCase for components, camelCase for hooks/utils (`useUsers.ts`)
- Export public API through `index.ts` barrels; keep internals private
- Colocate feature code — avoid cross-feature imports; use shared `components/` instead
- Routes/pages import from feature barrels, not deep paths

For good/bad examples, read `examples/rules/project-structure.md` when applying this rule.
